stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 750 Td
(Anti-Money Laundering \(AML\) Escalation Policy) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Apex Global Bank - Financial Crime Compliance) Tj T*
(Document ID: POL-AML-002 | Version 4.0 | Owner: Chief Compliance Officer) Tj T*
(Illustrative policy for the Finova demo workspace. Not legal or regulatory advice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Purpose) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This policy sets the mandatory thresholds and timelines for escalating suspicious activity) Tj T*
(detected by transaction monitoring, staff observation, or customer reports.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Mandatory Escalation Thresholds) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An alert must be escalated to the AML Investigations team when any of the following occur:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. A single cash deposit or withdrawal of INR 10,00,000 or more.) Tj T*
(2. Multiple cash transactions that together reach INR 10,00,000 or more within one calendar) Tj T*
(month \(structuring\).) Tj T*
(3. A cross-border transfer of USD 10,000 equivalent or more to or from a high-risk) Tj T*
(jurisdiction.) Tj T*
(4. A transaction monitoring risk score of 80 or above. These cases are also auto-frozen pending) Tj T*
(review.) Tj T*
(5. A risk score between 50 and 79 combined with any adverse media match or politically exposed) Tj T*
(person \(PEP\) flag.) Tj T*
(6. Rapid movement of funds: more than 80 percent of a credit moved out within 48 hours with no) Tj T*
(clear business purpose.) Tj T*
(7. Transactions inconsistent with the customer's declared income or business profile by more) Tj T*
(than 3 times.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Escalation Timeline) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- Level 1 \(Analyst\): reviews the alert within 24 hours and documents the rationale for closing) Tj T*
(or escalating.) Tj T*
(- Level 2 \(AML Investigations\): completes the investigation within 7 calendar days of) Tj T*
(escalation.) Tj T*
(- Level 3 \(Principal Officer\): decides whether to file a Suspicious Transaction Report \(STR\).) Tj T*
(An STR must be filed with the Financial Intelligence Unit within 7 days of the suspicion being) Tj T*
(confirmed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Account Freeze Rules) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- Risk score of 80 or above: debits are frozen automatically \(status "Frozen Escrow"\) until) Tj T*
(Level 2 clears or confirms the case.) Tj T*
(- A freeze longer than 30 days requires written approval from the Principal Officer.) Tj T*
(- Credits may continue to post to a frozen account unless law enforcement instructs otherwise.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Tipping-Off Prohibition) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Staff must never tell a customer that an alert, investigation or STR exists. Customer-facing) Tj T*
(teams use the neutral wording: "Your transaction is under routine review.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Record Keeping) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(All alerts, investigation notes and STR decisions are retained for 10 years. Closed alerts must) Tj T*
(contain a written rationale; "no issue found" alone is not acceptable.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7. Roles and Responsibilities) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
